{
  "appliance_id": "c3d8e4f0-8b1a-4f2c-a123-456789abcdef",
  "name": "PRP Node",
  "category": "guest",
  "description": "PRP (IEC 62439-3) RedBox simulation node for GNS3",
  "vendor_name": "Arctic3D AB",
  "vendor_url": "https://arctic3d.xyz",
  "product_name": "PRP Simulation Container",
  "registry_version": 6,
  "status": "experimental",
  "maintainer": "Arctic3D AB",
  "maintainer_email": "ceo@arctic3d.xyz",
  "usage": "# PRP Node\n\nIEC 62439-3 RedBox: a SAN (eth2, interlink) bridged onto two PRP LANs\n(eth0 = LAN A, eth1 = LAN B) or an HSR ring. Frames are duplicated with\nan RCT trailer / HSR tag, deduplicated on receive, and supervised with\n0x88FB frames. Open the console for logs and a periodic status line; the\ntelnet aux console (port 5000) gives a shell.\n\n## Environment variables\n\nSet these per node (right-click → Configure → General → Environment):\n\n| Variable | Default | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PRP_ROLE` | `prp-san` | `prp-san` (SAN → 2 PRP LANs; legacy `redbox`) · `hsr-san` (SAN → HSR ring) · `hsr-prp` (HSR ring → one PRP LAN) · `hsr-hsr` (QuadBox, follow-up) |\n| `HSR_PRP_ID` | `1` | NetId of the coupled PRP network (1-6); shared by both hsr-prp RedBoxes |\n| `HSR_LAN_ID` | `A` | PRP LAN the hsr-prp interlink attaches to: `A` or `B` |\n| `PRP_PRP_ID` | `0` | PRP network ID; 0 = auto-derive unique ID from hostname |\n| `PRP_LAN_A_IP` | (none) | Optional static IPv4 CIDR on LAN A (e.g. `10.1.0.10/24`) |\n| `PRP_LAN_B_IP` | (none) | Optional static IPv4 CIDR on LAN B |\n| `PRP_INTERLINK_IP` | (none) | Optional static IPv4 CIDR on the interlink/SAN |\n| `DEBUG_FRAMES` | (unset) | `1` = log every forwarded/dropped frame decision |\n| `PRP_CONFIG_PATH` | `/etc/prp/config.yaml` | Alternative config file |\n\n## HSR-PRP coupling (dual RedBox)\n\nPut two `hsr-prp` nodes on the same HSR ring: one with `HSR_LAN_ID=A`\nattached to PRP LAN A, one with `HSR_LAN_ID=B` attached to LAN B, both\nwith the same `HSR_PRP_ID`. PathId (NetId, LanId) prevents frames from\none PRP LAN being reinjected onto the other (IEC 62439-3 COR1 5.2.2.3.1).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Publisher → subscriber across the topology: subscriber console shows\n  `unique=` / `dupes=`; zero duplicates is the PRP/HSR proof.\n- Disconnect LAN A (or a ring link) — traffic continues seamlessly.\n",
  "docker": {
    "adapters": 3,
    "image": "ghcr.io/grymme/prp-sim:latest",
    "console_type": "telnet",
    "environment": "PRP_ROLE=redbox"
  },
  "symbols": {
    "default": "symbols/prp-node.svg"
  }
}
